==============================================================================
1. driver._classify -- BRANCH ORDER: issue codes outrank the provider markers
==============================================================================
  signature: (*, text: 'str', issue_codes: 'List[str]', contract_signal: 'bool', ambiguous: 'bool', no_reactions: 'bool', crashed: 'bool') -> 'str'
  _NETWORK_MARKERS matched by 'connection reset by peer': ['connection']
  _LLM_MARKERS matched by 'the model returned an empty completion': ['completion']
  ok network text  + no issue codes  -> failure_kind='network'  C-110 reads this as: CASUALTY
  ok llm text      + no issue codes  -> failure_kind='llm'  C-110 reads this as: CASUALTY
  !! network text  + ONE issue code  -> failure_kind='contract'  C-110 reads this as: DECLINE
  !! llm text      + ONE issue code  -> failure_kind='contract'  C-110 reads this as: DECLINE

  => A PROVIDER casualty carrying ANY issue code is written to the manifest
     as failure_kind='contract', which C-110 lists as a DECLARED DECLINE.

==============================================================================
2. KIND_UNKNOWN -- the shipped call site's status, message and codes
==============================================================================
_fail(
                outcome,
                status=_STATUS_FAIL,
                kind=KIND_UNKNOWN,
                message="no research report was produced and no reason was given",
                detail=joined,
                codes=codes,
            )
  KIND_UNKNOWN literal              : 'unknown'
  in C-110 _NC_INDETERMINATE_KINDS  : True
  in C-110 _NC_CASUALTY_KINDS       : False

==============================================================================
3. THE GUARD THAT LETS BOTH THROUGH
==============================================================================
    declared = (
    kind in _NC_DECLINE_KINDS
    or termination == SCIENTIFICALLY_UNRECOVERABLE
    or bool(codes)
    stated = bool(message) and declared
    if not declared and kind in _NC_INDETERMINATE_KINDS and not codes:

  `bool(codes)` alone satisfies `declared`, and the INDETERMINATE branch
  is guarded by `not codes` -- so one issue code both supplies the
  'stated reason' AND suppresses the indeterminate refusal.
